          "page": 5,
          "section": "3.4 The dissolution of the oxides and diffusion behavior of O during sintering",
          "quote": "As the edge of the Cr2O3 particle dissolves into the matrix, O2- ions diffuse, establishing a diffusion zone (as indicated by the black rectangle in Fig. 5 (d3)). This inward diffusion of O2- leads to a reduction in the concentration of Cr-O complex ions (Fig. 5 (c)) and a corresponding increase in the concentration of Cr atoms within the diffusion area (denoted by the black arrow in Fig. 5 (b) and the black rectangle in Fig. 5 (d2)).",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 5",
          "chunk_id": "6940cb94087a8ced:part:001"
